# Segmentation Form (DOC → Segment Engine)

Standalone React + TypeScript implementation of a client segmentation questionnaire.

## Run

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

## Build

```bash
npm run build
```

## Implemented requirements

- Component architecture:
  - `SegmentationForm`
    - `QualifiedBlock`
    - `ExperienceBlock`
    - `AmountBlock`
    - `GoalBlock`
    - `InstrumentsBlock`
    - `ResultPreview`
- Segmentation algorithm in `src/engine/calculateSegment.ts`
- Amount tiers for onboarding personalization
- JSON payload generation after submit
- UX states and validation rules for Continue button
- `navigateToOnboarding(segment, amountTier)` with segment-based route map
- Event tracking stubs in `src/analytics/trackEvent.ts`:
  - `segmentation_started`
  - `segmentation_completed`
  - `segment_novice` / `segment_advanced` / `segment_expert`
  - `amount_selected`
  - `goal_selected`

## Embed into page constructor (HTML block)

If you need to mount the segmentation form directly inside a constructor widget
(like on your screenshot), use:

- `embed/segmentation-widget.html`

Copy the full snippet into your HTML block.

Optional callbacks for integration:

```html
<script>
  window.navigateToOnboarding = function (segment, amountTier) {
    // your project router
  };

  window.onSegmentationComplete = function (payload) {
    // send payload to backend / CRM
  };
</script>
```

### Split by constructor fields (HTML / CSS / JS)

If your constructor has separate fields, use:

- HTML field: `embed/segmentation-widget.snippet.html`
- CSS field: `embed/segmentation-widget.snippet.css`
- JS field: `embed/segmentation-widget.snippet.js`

The JS file auto-initializes widgets on page load and also exposes
`window.initAllSegmentationWidgets()` for manual re-init after dynamic rendering.

## Single-script CDN widget (no HTML/CSS in constructor)

If you want the same integration style as tariff widget, use one script:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/filentio/finam@<COMMIT_SHA>/widget/finam-segmentation-widget.js?v=1"></script>
```

The script injects widget HTML + CSS automatically and mounts where the script tag is placed.

Optional target mount:

```html
<script
  src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/filentio/finam@<COMMIT_SHA>/widget/finam-segmentation-widget.js?v=1"
  data-target="#segmentation-widget-container"
></script>
```

Optional segment URL mapping (recommended for production routing):

```html
<script
  src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/filentio/finam@<COMMIT_SHA>/widget/finam-segmentation-widget.js?v=1"
  data-target="#segmentation-widget-container"
  data-onboarding-novice-url="/education/full-course/"
  data-onboarding-advanced-url="/education/short-course/"
  data-onboarding-expert-url="/education/expert-track/"
></script>
```

Notes:

- By default widget runs a single in-widget flow:
  анкета -> карточка результата -> встроенные шаги онбординга (без перехода на другую страницу).
- Inline онбординг отображается в формате stories: мобильный фрейм, сегментный прогресс-бар,
  навигация по тап-зонам (левая/правая части экрана).
- В stories добавлен sticky footer с CTA-кнопкой (всегда видна внизу) и
  градиентной подложкой для читаемости.
- Перед stories показывается transition-экран:
  "Мы подобрали для вас персональный маршрут" -> "Начать обучение".
- To force external redirect mode, set `data-onboarding-mode="external"`.
- If `data-onboarding-mode="auto"`, widget switches to external only when onboarding URLs are configured.
- In external mode fallback uses a safe hash navigation
  (`#finam-segmentation-onboarding?segment=...&amountTier=...`) to avoid hard redirects and route conflicts.
- Legacy global `window.navigateToOnboarding(...)` is disabled by default to prevent accidental conflicts.
- To enable legacy callback explicitly: `data-use-global-navigate="true"`.
- If third-party analytics scripts throw runtime/CORS errors, you can disable widget tracking hooks:
  `data-disable-tracking="true"`.
- You can define a common onboarding page URL via `data-onboarding-url="https://..."`.
  Widget will append `segment` and `amountTier` query params automatically.
- To open onboarding in a new tab, set `data-open-in-new-tab="true"`.

Public API:

- `window.FinamSegmentationWidget.mount(target, { replace?: boolean })`
- `window.FinamSegmentationWidget.initAll()`

Optional callbacks:

```html
<script>
  window.navigateToOnboarding = function (segment, amountTier) {
    // your app routing logic
  };

  window.onSegmentationComplete = function (payload) {
    // send payload to CRM/API
  };
</script>
```

## Onboarding module scaffold (from technical spec)

Added a dedicated feature module:

- `src/features/onboarding/Onboarding.tsx`
- `src/features/onboarding/OnboardingContext.tsx`
- `src/features/onboarding/hooks/*`
- `src/features/onboarding/screens/*`
- `src/features/onboarding/components/*`
- `src/features/onboarding/data/*`
- `src/features/onboarding/types/onboarding.ts`

Implemented in code:

- DOS typing, segmentation and amount tier mapping
- Track builder (`novice/advanced/expert`)
- Reducer-based onboarding state machine
- Risk scoring engine (DOS + Q5–Q8) with self-assessment cap
- Personalization helpers (content variants, highlighted instruments, portfolio/goal overlays)
- Base screen/component scaffolding for onboarding flow
